==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|embolus||piston|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|ἔμβολος||peg, stopper|tr=embolos|sc=polytonic|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɛmbələs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|emboli}}

# {{context|pathology|lang=en}} An obstruction causing an [[embolism]]: a [[blood clot]], air bubble or other matter carried by the [[blood stream]] and causing a blockage or [[occlusion]] of a [[blood vessel]].
# {{context|zoology|lang=en}} The structure on the end of the [[palp]] of male arachnids which contains the opening to the ejaculatory duct.
#*'''1996''', Michael J Roberts, ''Spiders of Britain and Northern Europe'', Collins 1996, p. 22:
#*:Those spiders with a simple bulb insert most of this; those with a complex palp insert only the '''embolus''', which in some species is very long [...].

